<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - Amplats year EPS, div slips.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Amplats year EPS, div slips.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		 162.8	 vs 190.3</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 120.0	 vs same</p>
<p>Analysts polled by Reuters predicted earnings per share in a range of 165.0-186.0 cents with consensus at 174.0 cents. They predicted a dividend of 122.5 cents/share in a range of 120.0-125.0 cents.</p>
<p>    Net income		289.1	 vs 319.5</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   358.6	 vs 397.7</p>
<p>    Tax			 69.5	  vs  78.2</p>
<p>    Associates		126.8	 vs 214.8</p>
<p>    Divs from other invests 154.8*    vs 124.4</p>
<p>    Net fee and other income 77.0     vs 58.5</p>
<p>Div payable Sept 17</p>
<p>on register Aug 29</p>
<p>Full name: Anglo American Platinum Corp Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - * includes dividends from diamond operations.</p>
<p>Amplats said lower earnings were due to a strike at Rustenburg in May and higher operating costs at Potgietersrust Platinum Ltd and Lebowa Platinum Mines Ltd.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
